<section class="trademark-reference section-space">
    <div class="container site-container">
        <div class="row gy-5 gx-lg-5">
            <main class="col-lg-8">
                <p class="lead-copy">A strong trademark is an important business asset. Sonagra &amp; Company assists businesses, promoters and brand owners with trademark searches, applications, prosecution and related ownership documentation.</p>
                <p>Our support is designed to help clients make informed decisions before adopting a mark and to manage the registration and protection process with clear documentation and timely follow-up.</p>

                <div class="trademark-reference-list">
                    <div class="trademark-reference-item"><span>01</span><p>Conducting expansive trademark searches to assess existing marks, possible conflicts and registration considerations before a brand is adopted.</p></div>
                    <div class="trademark-reference-item"><span>02</span><p>Drafting and filing trademark applications with the appropriate details, classifications and supporting documents.</p></div>
                    <div class="trademark-reference-item"><span>03</span><p>Follow-up and prosecution of trademark applications, including tracking application progress and assisting with responses to registry communications.</p></div>
                    <div class="trademark-reference-item"><span>04</span><p>Appearing and representing clients before the official Trademark Registry for hearings, objections and other application-related proceedings.</p></div>
                    <div class="trademark-reference-item"><span>05</span><p>Drafting and filing assignment deeds and related documents for the transfer, licensing or reorganisation of trademark rights.</p></div>
                    <div class="trademark-reference-item"><span>06</span><p>Transfer of ownership of trademarks, including documentation and procedural support for recording the change with the relevant authority.</p></div>
                </div>
            </main>

